WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:01.470
- Welcome back.

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:04.110
I'm Taraji Henson, filling
in for Kelly today.

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:07.840
If you know me, you know
I'm a huge animal lover.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.440
So I'm very excited about my next guest.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:11.390
They're a family

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:14.400
of animal lovers from
down under. (chuckles)

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.290
They're also the stars of
Crikey! It's the Irwins,

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:20.110
which is back for season four

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:22.849
on Animal Planet and Discovery Plus.

00:00:22.849 --> 00:00:23.860
(birds chirping)

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:27.670
- [Bindi] I love that everyday
brings a new happy moment.

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:29.040
A new challenge.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:29.873
- Look, Grace.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:31.770
There's Africa!

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.350
- Can you see the rhinos out there?

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:34.803
They've spotted you.

00:00:34.803 --> 00:00:36.586
- This would be the ultimate Lion King.

00:00:36.586 --> 00:00:37.419
- It actually would.

00:00:37.419 --> 00:00:38.252
- Actually would be

00:00:38.252 --> 00:00:39.740
pretty awesome.
- Let's go to pride rock.

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:42.280
- I've never worried so much in my life.

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:44.040
Okay, there's a buggy coming.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.880
- She's so sleepy.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:50.310
- Because I want her to be
absolutely healthy and happy

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:51.400
a hundred percent of the time.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.683
- Who is that?

00:00:52.683 --> 00:00:54.440
Who is that?

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:55.273
Ooh.

00:00:55.273 --> 00:00:56.106
(audience clapping)

00:00:56.106 --> 00:01:00.106
- Please welcome Terri,
Bindi and Robert Irwin.

00:01:00.106 --> 00:01:03.116
Welcome!
(music band flourishing)

00:01:03.116 --> 00:01:04.390
What do you have there?

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:05.518
- It's a little tortoise, here.

00:01:05.518 --> 00:01:06.351
Isn't he cute?

00:01:06.351 --> 00:01:07.188
He's so good.
- Oh my goodness.

00:01:07.188 --> 00:01:08.220
- And a little echidna

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.055
over there as well.
- Yep, yep.

00:01:09.055 --> 00:01:10.326
I've got an echidna.

00:01:10.326 --> 00:01:13.030
Echidnas are actually
related to the platypus,

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:14.610
so they're egg laying mammals.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:15.623
They're pretty cute.

00:01:15.623 --> 00:01:17.100
- Oh my goodness--
(bird chirping)

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.829
Who's making that noise?

00:01:18.829 --> 00:01:21.260
- (laughs) We have lots
of birds behind us.

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:24.940
We're actually at our beautiful
wildlife sanctuary here,

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:26.300
which is really special.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:29.370
And so our gardens are
filled with animals roaming

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:31.090
and that's what you can
hear in the background.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:32.080
- [Taraji] Oh my goodness.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:33.000
I wish I was there.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.990
It looks so peaceful.

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:37.050
Your little baby is so cute.

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:40.150
Does she have a favorite
animal at the zoo?

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:41.760
- She does, actually.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:43.810
My beautiful daughter is so sweet.

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:44.860
She loves all animals,

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:47.610
but actually her favorites are tortoises.

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:48.850
She likes tortoises.

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:50.630
These guys are the elongated tortoises,

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:53.910
but she likes the giant Aldabra tortoises.

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:56.550
We have one tortoise named Igloo,

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:58.340
and these tortoises are huge.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:01:59.580
Like, they come up to my hip.

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:00.840
They're massive.
(Robert laughing)

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:03.520
They're like these giant tortoise whales,

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:05.900
and Igloo is her best friend.
- Wow.

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:08.530
- She goes up to Igloo
and tries to pat him,

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:10.342
and he runs to her.

00:02:10.342 --> 00:02:11.337
- It's adorable.
- Which is quite slow,

00:02:11.337 --> 00:02:12.760
but really cute to see.
- Yes!

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:14.780
- They have this adorable bond.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.530
I know, I love that my
daughter's best friend

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:17.410
is a giant tortoise.

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:18.750
It's hilarious. (laughs)

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:21.100
- Well, I'm a fan of
your daughter's cheeks.

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:23.008
She has the juiciest cheeks.

00:02:23.008 --> 00:02:23.937
(Taraji laughing)
- (laughs) Thank you.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.490
- She is very squishy.
- Oh my goodness.

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:32.040
You did something special in
your daughter's honor recently.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.260
What was it?

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:34.990
- I did actually.

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:37.510
When beautiful Grace Warrior was born,

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:41.190
my first words were that
she's our graceful warrior,

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:43.670
and that's actually how she got her name.

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:45.470
And so in her honor,

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:49.320
I got graceful warrior tattooed on my arm

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:51.020
in my dad's handwriting.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.530
(Taraji cooing)
So that my beautiful daughter

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:56.860
and my dad could always be
together and be with me.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:58.610
And I think it's really special

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:01.180
to have them close to me always,

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:02.480
no matter what happens in life.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:04.210
And so I'm really blessed.
(audience clapping)

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:05.680
I have such a wonderful family,

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:07.810
and I feel like dad is always with us

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:09.190
in everything that we do.

00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:10.280
- That is so beautiful.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:13.160
I also have my son's
name tattooed right here

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:15.109
on the vein that leads to my heart.

00:03:15.109 --> 00:03:15.947
- [Robert] Beautiful.

00:03:15.947 --> 00:03:17.040
- Exactly!

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:18.632
- [Taraji] Yeah, so I understand.

00:03:18.632 --> 00:03:19.920
- So special.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:21.720
- And Robert, you just turned 18,

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.950
so you're officially a grown man.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:25.380
How did you celebrate?

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:26.890
- I know!

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:27.810
Isn't that crazy?

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.610
Yeah, it's a huge milestone.

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:30.900
It feels very surreal.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.950
It was a really wonderful
little celebration at the zoo

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:36.080
just with friends and family here at home,

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:37.850
but it is definitely really exciting.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:39.256
You know, wildlife conservation

00:03:39.256 --> 00:03:40.730
is everything to us.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:42.810
Protecting our world wildlife,

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:43.830
and now turning 18,

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:45.238
I get to be more stuck in

00:03:45.238 --> 00:03:48.230
with all of the different
conservation work that we do

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:49.380
around the world.

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:50.920
So it really is a big honor

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:52.300
for me to get to work full time

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:54.790
and enter this wonderful
new chapter of life.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.456
It's really exciting.

00:03:56.456 --> 00:03:59.077
I'm very, very proud, definitely.

00:03:59.077 --> 00:04:00.810
- Congratulations.

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:01.855
Congratulations.
(audience clapping)

00:04:01.855 --> 00:04:05.330
Terri, this new season covers a lot.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:06.960
What can people expect?

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:11.060
- Well, we are just going hammer and tong

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:12.930
over here at Australia zoo.

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:15.110
We've got a beautiful wildlife hospital

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:18.060
where we've treated over 110,000 animals,

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:20.700
so it's a lot of action with echidnas.

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:22.260
I don't know what the deal was,

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:25.760
but we just kept getting
little orphaned echidnas in,

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:28.760
and we raised them up and
released them back to the wild,

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:31.350
but it's all the dramas of raising babies.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:34.340
And when the echidnas are tiny,

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.260
when they first hatch out of the egg,

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:39.540
they look kind of like jelly bean blobs.

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:40.970
They're really funny.
- They're hilarious.

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:43.210
- They don't have any spikes,
and they're really weird,

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:45.120
and that's kind of fun to see.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:48.260
And then, of course, it's
keeping our animals happy.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.600
So it's making sure they
have beautiful homes

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.810
and wonderful environments to live in.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:55.150
And it's all the dramas

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:58.890
of reconstructing beautiful habitat areas,

00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:00.885
and you were moving alligators.

00:05:00.885 --> 00:05:02.900
- A lot of animal rescues as well.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.280
A lot of what we do is going
out and rescuing animals

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.400
that are in need.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:07.500
So there's some

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:11.440
really exciting, scary,
heart-pounding moments

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:13.640
and some special family times as well.

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:15.080
It's a very personal look

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:18.580
into to how we continue this
incredible wildlife legacy.

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:20.288
Yeah, I think Grace is
the star of the show.

00:05:20.288 --> 00:05:21.121
- [Bindi And Robert] She is.

00:05:21.121 --> 00:05:21.954
- I'm sure.

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:24.283
She's stalling with those
cheeks, I'll tell you that.

00:05:24.283 --> 00:05:26.060
(audience clapping)
And when I come to Australia,

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:27.260
I'm coming.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.790
I'm coming to visit you guys.

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:29.623
- Yes.
- Yes!

00:05:29.623 --> 00:05:31.640
- Definitely.
- Definitely do.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:32.990
- You're a wildlife warrior.

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:33.823
- Always welcome.

00:05:33.823 --> 00:05:34.738
- Yes!

00:05:34.738 --> 00:05:36.251
Take care, and I'm coming for Grace!

00:05:36.251 --> 00:05:37.608
'Cause I wanna see those cheeks!

00:05:37.608 --> 00:05:41.130
(Taraji laughing)
- Yes! (laughs)

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:42.553
- Take care, stay safe.

